WEBVTT

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.270
Where are you coming from?

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.320
From Cantar. We left because they decided
to surrender to the Empire.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:14.280
They said the Empire was going to take
all of our food.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.280
Sure, they'll guarantee our safety,

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:18.540
but we would've starved to death there.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.540
But is there a country that would accept
this many refugees?

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.750
Chielo might.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:26.960
Chielo?

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.500
The Cage of Paradise

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:42.020
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:02.220
MARCH 3RD, TORQYEAN CALENDAR YEAR 76
CHIELO

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:07.100
Mahmut! Just how much longer
do we have to climb?

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.690
You can do it. Our destination is that tower.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.190
My knees hurt too much to walk!

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.530
Let's call it a day and stay at this inn.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.990
We've only been walking for three hours!

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:22.370
Whose idea was it to build a city
in a place like this?

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:26.000
It is because there used to be
an almshouse on this mountain.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.710
Almshouse?

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:31.670
A welfare institution that would provide food
and shelter to the poor,

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.460
or treatment for the seriously ill.

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:39.300
Twelve hundred years ago,
the political refugees

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:43.260
who gathered at
the almshouse created a community,

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.770
which was how the Republic of Chielo
was founded.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:51.850
Thus, even now, this nation's head of state's
title is director. It is a remnant from that period.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.360
I see.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.860
So... Wait! Hold on!

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:59.820
Apparently, they've never been invaded
in their 1200 years of history.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.460
What is it? A play?

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.000
It's a fable known as The Key of Heaven.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:18.420
In these parts, good people go to an eternal paradise
called Chielo after death,

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:22.890
and bad people are imprisoned in the dark lands
of Fondo where no light can reach.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.350
And this play is based on that.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.770
The leader of a group of bandits does one good deed
right before he dies

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:34.810
and receives the key to Chielo from the gatekeeper
of the underworld as a reward.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:39.690
One key only grants one person entry through the gate.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.740
Those wandering around Fondo get wind of this
and rush the leader,

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:49.080
and the story ends with the key being lost
in the commotion.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.210
There's no helping them.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:52.920
However,

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:58.250
the leader places the key in his breast pocket
and steals thousands of keys from the gatekeeper.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:03.220
Then with a great big swing,
he throws them all across Fondo!

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:13.310
The leader brings his bandits and the people
sent to Fondo together and leads them into Chielo.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.440
Final feliz.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.280
Final feliz?

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.610
It means they lived happily ever after.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.820
Hey, Carbajal!

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:28.030
Stop making changes to the script!

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.290
How could you have him take the murderers to Chielo?

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.120
Don't they deserve pity?

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.420
Everyone needs to have a final feliz ending.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.210
Director Carbajal.

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:43.050
It is time for your meeting with the foreign emissaries.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.680
Already?

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.550
Sorry, we'll talk about this another time.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.260
Let's go, Casandra.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:50.560
Director?

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.520
See you again, director.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:55.690
I want to see The Three Donkeys next time!

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.020
Excuse me.

00:04:58.610 --> 00:05:02.900
Are you the leader of the Republic of Chielo?

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:09.450
Chielo has a strong welfare program.

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:11.950
But it's got to cost a lot of money.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:15.830
This country still has a strong sense of charity,

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:21.920
and we provide free assistance to the poor
and sick who seek our help.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.970
How can a country afford to do that?

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.260
South Rumeriana has a culture of giving

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:31.680
where the wealthy give donations
to the poor and public institutions.

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:35.980
Those who give donations receive
a great amount of respect.

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:41.190
It encourages rising nobles and great merchants
alike to give donations.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.990
Furthermore, Chielo has a mild climate
that allows for rich agriculture.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:46.860
We even have a good port.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.990
Coupled with our citizen's modest tastes,
we have more than plenty.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:54.620
Here we are. This is the assembly hall.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.630
This assembly hall has been converted
from the original almshouse built here.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:03.500
What's going on?

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.260
We have more visitors than usual today.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:09.220
Oh, director. This way please.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:15.600
They are all refugees whose food stores were
taken from them by the Empire.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:18.940
Representatives have come here seeking
Chielo's protection.

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:21.980
There are over 30,000 refugees outside our gates.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.770
Thirty thousand?

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.360
I did not notice them at all.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:31.070
That is because they are on the opposite side
of the gate we brought you through.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:35.450
Casandra, please begin moving them into the city.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.250
Understood.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:39.370
What? Are you sure?

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:43.590
Taking in refugees would mean making
an enemy of the Empire.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:46.510
If that happens, you'll have defend against a siege here.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:49.630
If you include all the refugees,

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.430
you'll be lucky if your stores last three months.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:55.180
If we close our doors to them here and now,

00:06:55.350 --> 00:07:00.230
these people will starve to death with the feeling
that the whole world turned its back on them.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:04.650
That is far from a final feliz happy ending.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:08.400
Even though they may still die,

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:12.910
if it means making their final moments peaceful,
then that's something we can do.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:15.330
The almshouse that was the precursor to Chielo

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:19.210
was built with the goal of bringing final feliz endings
to those without hope.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:23.290
If someone means to interfere with our mission,

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:25.000
then Chielo will fight,

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.630
no matter who the enemy is.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.670
In that case,

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.300
please join our alliance.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:38.560
Last month, Torqye, Urado, and Venedik
formed a military alliance.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:42.520
Many nations across the continent
have joined our alliance.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:47.940
Fiore, Humo, Seallant, Espada and Tauro.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:51.030
If we are able to join hands with Chielo as well,

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:56.410
we'll be able to complete our bulwark against the Empire
formed by our anti-Imperial alliance.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:01.910
I see, so you would like to put Chielo on the frontlines
of the anti-Imperial alliance.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:05.250
Yes, all in order to end the war.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.300
That sounds very promising.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:13.800
The thought of gaining so many allies at once.

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:17.300
As long as there are people in need of Chielo,

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:20.560
we cannot allow Chielo to disappear.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:24.060
So why don't we have them help ensure
that never happens?

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.810
We're counting on you, Mahmut.

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.820
13 DAYS LATER
NINA

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:35.780
General Pino, apparently the main Torqyean army
is on the move.

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:41.790
I think it's time we get off our laurels and pick up
where we left off with establishing a world empire.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:44.120
The enemy commander is Halil Pasha.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.710
I have heard he's entered Tauro City.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.500
If you are able to crush
this so-called anti-Imperial alliance,

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:54.510
I am sure it would greatly please Minister Louis.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:57.260
MARCH 22TH, TORQYEAN CALENDAR YEAR 76
TAURO CITY

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.720
To think it would be this much trouble.

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:05.480
I certainly underestimated the hate Cuore di Rumeriana
has for Torqye.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:09.150
Did one of the Cuorians do something?

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:13.900
We're only allowed to take the streets
that run around the large cities.

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:16.860
I never thought this would be straightforward,

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:18.910
but to think it would be this bad...

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.790
Your march has been slowed to a crawl,

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:24.830
and made to go the long way around.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:30.460
You're the descendants of the war party that wreaked
havoc on these lands 500 years ago.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:35.880
I'm sure it wouldn't sit right with those Cuore weaklings
to have you running around their cities.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:39.890
But now you're in our territory.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:43.890
We've already arranged for your armies
to be able to march at full speed.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.140
-Show Rumeriana the legendary speed...
-Show Rumeriana the legendary speed...

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:48.480
-of the Torqyean march.
-of the Torqyean march.

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:51.270
I don't know how I can thank you.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:54.280
It looks like we'll be able to get my 6000 soldiers

00:09:54.440 --> 00:10:00.490
as well as the 20,000 additional soldiers marching behind
us to Chielo before the Empire's army arrives.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.740
Halil Pasha, you have guests.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.710
I was the kulak in Campana.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.630
My name is Blanca.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.550
Having heard you were here,

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.800
I have come for an audience.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.630
From Campana?

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.550
I see, that must have been quite an ordeal.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.300
This boy too?

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.640
I worked in a foundry in Campana.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:27.100
I am Vasco.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:34.440
I promise we are here to help you from now on
if there's anything you need.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:39.160
Then I have a favor to ask of you.

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:44.030
I have something I'd like to show you,
Halil Pasha.

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:50.040
This is a giant shark ray.

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:53.210
Did you design this?

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:58.010
Yes, when I showed it to my boss,
he made me promise not to show anyone,

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:00.130
and he even took the blueprint from me.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:03.050
But now I understand why!

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:07.640
It means we can create a weapon that will change
the way wars are fought, doesn't it?

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:11.810
Building this is impossible, Vasco.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.440
I'm sorry we weren't able to help you.

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:16.610
Take this with you.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.320
It's a pass.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:22.990
You'll be able to stay at any inn within the alliance,
and trade out your horse for free.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.280
Please wait!

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:26.790
We could eradicate our enemies with this!

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:31.120
It is not our objective to kill
as many people as possible in this war.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.330
But...

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:35.460
I'm sure there is another use for this technology.

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:39.510
For example, it could be helpful
in a large construction project.

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:44.010
Once the war ends, what do you think
about using it for reconstruction?

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:47.180
All the more reason to use it now!

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:50.520
This has the power to end the war quickly.

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:54.100
Do you not think this is too powerful?

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:57.360
It is too dangerous to use for war.

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:01.450
You should forget about it for now until the time comes.

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:04.910
Halil Pasha, it's the Empire!

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:07.120
Their main force has moved out of Nina!

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:09.870
What did you say? Where are they headed?

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.330
They are marching towards a coastal path.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:13.870
Chielo!

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:17.090
Blanca, Vasco, please excuse me!

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:23.840
All forces, move out!

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.890
We had fun, Halil Pasha.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:31.060
Let's drink again when this fighting is over!

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:35.440
I'm sorry you didn't get the answer you were hoping for.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:39.230
I'm glad I made a copy.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:42.440
I know I can avenge everyone with this.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:45.450
CHIELO
MAYORGA ORPHANAGE

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:46.660
So they've made a move.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:52.000
Seventy thousand Imperial soldiers are currently
in Salu territory and making way toward Chielo.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:54.330
Salu surrendered immediately.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:12:58.960
The Imperial forces should arrive near
Chielo in three days.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:01.170
Even if you included local militias,

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:05.340
the total forces of Espada, Seallant and Humo would
only be around 10,000.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:09.970
The Imperial forces could conquer all three cities
simultaneously if they wanted.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:13.600
They do not wish to needlessly expand the warfront.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:17.810
The Imperial general has a sound strategy.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:20.690
The militia squad report to me!

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:26.110
Volunteer refugee soldiers report to Draco district,
and Chielo volunteers report to Cetos district.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.160
Get a representative in each squad to create a registry.

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:31.120
Hey, Carbajal!

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:36.170
We might just be a group of citizens and refugees,
but there are 23,000 of us all together!

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:39.130
We might be amateurs, but we've got high morale!

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:42.420
This is the first time I've seen such a lively war.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:44.840
There's clearly way too many people.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:49.140
Getting a bunch of farm hands together
isn't going to be much help.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:50.850
It's okay.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:52.430
Chielo has a giant cage

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:58.480
to capture any bad monster
that's decided to attack our city.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:03.230
So there's nothing you need to worry about.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:05.240
TWO DAYS LATER

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:07.650
A few thousand cavalry troops
along the Espada border!

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.410
Director.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.240
The Torqyean army has arrived.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:16.250
Halil Pasha!

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:20.040
It is good to see you, Halil Pasha.

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:21.920
We managed to make it in time.

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:23.500
Everyone.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:25.460
Please come inside the castle.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:29.340
No, we'll make camp here if that's okay.

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:30.510
But...

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.180
Torqyeans are equestrian tribesmen.

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:38.230
We have lived our lives running freely over the plains.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.270
Isn't that right?

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:43.610
The Imperial Army is almost here as well.

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:46.190
They should arrive sometime around tomorrow evening.

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:47.990
Mahmut.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:53.240
You truly have created a wonderful path for all of us.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:55.660
MARCH 25TH, TORQYEAN CALENDAR YEAR 76
SALU AND CHIELO'S BORDER

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.660
Oh, wild strawberries!

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:58.910
BALT-RHEIN EMPIRE LAND ARMY, 2ND DIVISION
ARMY LIEUTENANT GENERAL ANTON ADAM

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:01.420
Chielo's spring comes earlier than the Empire.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:03.670
BALT-RHEIN EMPIRE LAND ARMY, 1ST DIVISION
LIEUTENANT GENERAL JOHAN FRENTZEN

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:08.920
Frentzen? This is the end of the line.
Your army corps should have arrived in Chielo by now.

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:11.680
My stomach isn't feeling well.

00:15:11.840 --> 00:15:15.390
Don't push yourself too hard.
You've always had health issues.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:18.430
You must have gotten nauseous
from crossing the rope bridge.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.230
What is it, Frentzen?

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:24.900
What was that?

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.610
Could this be Chielo's work?

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:33.620
It will take 20 days to rebuild the bridge.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:39.910
If so, we won't be able to make contact
or get supplies from the back lines.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:44.460
Our march to Chielo has taken us
to Fondo instead.

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.340
NEXT DAY
26TH, EARLY MORNING

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:51.050
The Imperial forces number 67,000.
That is quite a large number.

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:56.050
Having that many soldiers means they'll need that much
more bread to feed them.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:00.600
There is something nice about wooden houses.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:05.230
I've never seen so many wooden houses
lined up next to each other.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:09.150
It's difficult for large trees to grow in such a dry climate.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:12.650
So building them from wood must have
cost a lot of money.

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:14.570
Chielo is famous for them.

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:18.830
The Nada royal family donated cedar trees
to Chielo to build their houses.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:22.330
In any case, just like all the surrounding villages,

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.170
I haven't seen a single soul around.

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:27.920
Chielo has rejected surrender.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:31.800
They've apparently let in all the residents
around the area.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:35.140
We won't be able to commandeer
their resources like we've been doing.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.390
With our supply lines cut,

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:41.230
it's almost like we're the ones under siege.

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.560
There is no need to worry.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:47.060
That is what the Phoinike armada is for.

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:51.860
We're very fortunate that the supplies from Phoinike
have arrived on schedule.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:54.400
BALT-RHEIN EMPIRE LAND ARMY, 12 DIVISION
LIEUTENANT GENERAL CHRISTHALD BALZ

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.410
Although they won't be able to make another delivery
until after the autumn harvest.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:04.210
General Pino himself has entrusted this important
transport to our 12th Division.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:09.630
We will do whatever it takes to get these provisions
to General Pino.

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:13.510
Our target is this transport division.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:16.220
This tactic can only be used once.

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:19.010
This is our first and final plan.

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:22.980
I'm counting on you, gentlemen. Put an end to this war.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.350
26TH MIDNIGHT
CHIELO, SALU'S GATE

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:28.980
Lord Balz,

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:35.490
roughly 10,000 infantrymen have emerged
from the Salu gate and are approaching from our left.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:39.240
The enemy? So they've come to steal
our supplies already.

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:42.410
The enemy is likely a Chielo militia.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:46.420
Twelfth Division, create a formation along our rear!

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:48.750
-Charge!
-Ready!

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:57.930
Lord Balz, in front of our packhorses!

00:17:58.090 --> 00:17:59.640
Launch javelins!

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:04.640
-We're being attacked from the front!
-Change formation! Target the cavalry!

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:11.480
All right, their provisions are ours!
Hurry up, you bastards!

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:14.780
Take everything we can before the main--

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.610
I guess the jig is up.

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:19.820
All forces, fall back! Light them up!

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.540
Put them out!

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:28.500
Squad 56, Squad 57, don't let them get away!

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:32.040
If we fail here, we fail General Pino!

00:18:32.210 --> 00:18:34.090
Fire the arrows!

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.920
Whatever happens, don't drop the supplies!

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:39.340
Hold here.

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:41.800
This doesn't call for reinforcements.

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:45.890
They're back! Open the gate!

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.020
Cavalry, follow me!

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:54.520
Squads 58, 59 and 60 on me!

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:57.030
We'll never get an opportunity like this again!

00:18:57.190 --> 00:19:00.530
We'll take Haubia Gate, and make up for our failings!

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:06.540
Take the gate tower!
Don't let them drop the gate!

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:11.540
General Pino, 12th Division's flag has just been raised
over Haubia Gate!

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:14.210
We'll be able to storm the city now!

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:18.590
All forces march! We are storming the city
through Haubia Gate.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:20.760
Hit them hard!

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:33.480
They're all surging into Chielo.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:37.030
I'm so tempted to attack them from behind.

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.490
It would be so easy.

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:40.900
No, Abbas. We're to stand by.

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:43.700
Yes, lock as many enemies inside the cage as possible.

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:47.450
Our role in this is yet to come.
I know that this is all the plan.

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:50.120
But this is such an amazing opportunity.

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:51.500
They've stopped!

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:53.790
Two army corps have entered.

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.000
I'd say they total about 10,000 men.

00:19:56.210 --> 00:20:01.470
Maybe the enemy got wise because you said something
about attacking them from behind.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:06.640
It seems the Empire has someone
with sharp senses on their side.

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:10.020
The 1st Division has stopped.

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:11.890
What did you say?

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:14.520
Frentzen stopped his division?

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:19.440
Did his instincts he's so proud of
warn him of some danger?

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.650
Lord Balz.

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:23.160
There is no need for worry.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:28.540
The only sound in the old town district
is the footsteps of our Imperial army.

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.620
There's no ambush waiting for us
in the new district.

00:20:31.830 --> 00:20:34.040
You're right, Jurgen.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:36.170
Leave the cowards behind.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:40.510
The 12th Division will take all the glory ourselves!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:47.300
I guess all we managed to get was
one of the monster's arms.

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:48.890
Pour the oil!

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:50.770
Go! March!

00:20:50.930 --> 00:20:53.020
Oil? Oh, no!

00:20:57.360 --> 00:21:00.030
-It's a wave of fire!
-Run!

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.860
It's too late! Help me!

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:19.880
This isn't good.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:21.590
Hey, Mahmut.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:26.430
Is there any way we can kill the rest of the Imperial
soldiers that are left outside the walls?

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:31.060
The wooden houses unbecoming of the local aesthetics.

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:35.890
Those houses were built to be burned
down from the very start.

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:38.360
If you hadn't stopped the general,

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:40.610
we would be in there too right now.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:45.900
It is what Chielo was prepared to do
in order to protect their people.

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:51.410
This is the truth behind their legend
of 1,200 years without defeat.

00:21:51.580 --> 00:21:53.790
But now they are out of moves.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:58.920
Their only chance at winning was to eradicate
all of us with this gambit.

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:03.510
Leave 20,000 men behind for the Torqyean army,
and station the rest in front of each gate.

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:06.170
We will completely blockade the city.

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:11.220
Let Chielo suffocate under the thousands of
refugees they've let inside.

00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:15.270
It is time to put an end to this country's legend!

00:23:48.280 --> 00:23:51.320
I see it won't be so easy.

00:23:51.490 --> 00:23:53.620
But this is a path Mahmut carved out for us.

00:23:53.780 --> 00:23:56.280
It's up to me to see it through.

00:23:56.450 --> 00:23:59.290
Next time, "Distant Funeral Bells."

00:23:59.450 --> 00:24:01.580
I will also do everything I can.
